& [WhyNow] is prerequisite completion plus explicit continued-work authority
  + [embedded_core_gate] passed through CEB-001 to CEB-015
  + [service_gate] passed through resident service, service-backed MCP, and supervised local lifecycle
  + [signed_frontier] names phase_1_mock_loop as the first supervised-runtime manifestation
  + [current_source] asks the active conversation to continue productive Cantor work for a four-hour shift

& [WhyThisShape] is the smallest proof-bearing ecosystem
  + [new_crate] keeps ecosystem protocol responsibilities separate from cantor_core semantics and cantor_service transport
  + [logical_time] makes expiry and deadline behavior exactly replayable
  + [caller_supplied_identity] avoids nondeterministic UUID generation
  + [typed_envelope] makes message intent, addressing, authority, and payload inspectable
  + [append_only_transcript] preserves causal proof without selecting persistence prematurely
  + [mock_adapters] prove the seam before official live Codex interface dependencies are selected
  + [deterministic_Observer] proves acceptance gates without claiming full faculty or provider inference
  + [no_effects] proves semantic approval remains distinct from exterior authorization

& [Alternatives] records bounded rejection
  + [live_Codex_first] is rejected because transport truth would obscure unproven message and authority semantics
  + [extend_cantor_service] is rejected because local semantic transport and supervised agent protocol have different responsibility boundaries
  + [general_agent_framework] is rejected because Phase 1 needs exactly one bounded cycle
  + [persistent_database_now] is deferred until transcript access, recovery, and concurrency requirements are measured
  + [async_runtime_now] is rejected because no concurrent or external wait exists in the deterministic mock profile
  + [full_faculty_runtime] is deferred because deterministic policy checks are sufficient for this acceptance boundary

& [Premortem] records principal failure paths
  + [failure] is a message accepted for the wrong participant
    + [mitigation] is exact role-plus-identity recipient admission
  + [failure] is manager or worker expands its authority
    + [mitigation] is subset validation against commission and work packet before append
  + [failure] is duplicate or cyclic messages appear as progress
    + [mitigation] is message, idempotency, and semantic-fingerprint indexes
  + [failure] is fixture passes by approving an effect request
    + [mitigation] is non-waivable empty-effect review and no EffectBroker implementation
  + [failure] is mock success misreported as live Codex capability
    + [mitigation] is explicit SML-011 boundary in specification, crate docs, proof, narrative, and support matrix

& [InvalidationCondition] is any implementation that introduces live Codex, provider, process, persistence, notification, multi-worker, promotion, or effect behavior under this signature
